  "existing_acceptance_limits": [
    "The cleanup unit matrix uses temporary files across old versions and layouts. Its expectation that installer cache files disappear must change deliberately under the new default preservation policy.",
    "Qt tests cover editable and busy refusals, cooperative restart, close veto, removal ordering and optional user environments. They do not verify an actual old-to-new Windows GUI launch.",
    "Updater tests pin the offered version and reject a stale metadata readback. They do not test new metadata with older imported code.",
    "The online Windows workflow checks a fresh current installation, backend, dependencies and uv behavior. It does not test multiple old installations, conflicting inherited version overrides, preserved caches and actual Desktop or Start Menu launch receipts together."
  ],
  "required_upgrade_scenario_tests": [
    "New requested release with an old SPACR_PACKAGE_SPEC, older offline bundle and explicit development override: reject or clearly report the conflict before deletion.",
    "New metadata with old imported code through PYTHONPATH, user-site or competing distribution metadata: reject false success and verify the actual relaunched GUI.",
    "Multiple per-user, frozen all-users and custom installer roots: discover owned instances and repair owned links while keeping user environments and checkouts by default.",
    "Sentinel caches, models, demos, settings, datasets, backend environments and unrelated temporary files inside and outside install roots: preserve every byte by default, including custom configured paths and junctions.",
    "Default-off cache GUI showing folder contents, counts, sizes and purpose: delete only explicitly selected owned cache folders; cancellation changes nothing.",
    "Failures during bootstrap, dependency download, validation, activation or launch: keep the old working runtime or provide a verified rollback and preserve all persistent files.",
    "Disposable Windows VM acceptance: install an old release, update using NSIS and the app, and verify Desktop, Start Menu, command and GUI receipts for versions, executable, prefix and package file. No existing user installation is modified without explicit authorization.",
